{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.OrthoschemeTiling","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.OrthoschemeTiling","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.OrthoschemeLambdaSum"],"declarations":23,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.inscribedTriangle_vertex_incidence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.inscribedTriangle_vertex_incidence","kind":"theorem","line":469,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeTiling.lean#L469-L536","doc":"**Vertex incidence.**  Each of the three circle points lies ON two chord\nlines and STRICTLY INSIDE the third half-plane.\n\nThis is what pins `inscribedTriangle` to the triangle whose vertices are the\nthree named points of the circle.  Strictness in the third slot is where\n`0 < R` is spent: the gap is `2R·sin·sin`.\n\n**No acuteness.**  This statement held for every positive triple summing to `π`\nall along; the three `< π/2` hypotheses it used to carry were inherited from its\nneighbours and were consumed by nothing (dropped 2026-09-08, bean `qou-w3eg`).\nEach is spent only inside a `Real.sin_pos_of_pos_of_lt_pi` whose side goal is\n`X < π`, and `α + β + γ = π` with the other two positive already gives that.\nThe gap `cos ψ' − cos(2ψ+ψ') = 2 sin(ψ+ψ') sin ψ` is positive whenever both\nsines are, which on the simplex is everywhere.\n\nThat matters downstream rather than here: this lemma is the only place the\n`idealTet_eq_chimney` chain touched acuteness, so its removal carries the\nvertex-defined-region identity to obtuse triangles as well. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.hypVolume_chimney_inscribedTriangle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.hypVolume_chimney_inscribedTriangle","kind":"theorem","line":421,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeTiling.lean#L421-L455","doc":"**Milnor's Λ-sum, on the inscribed triangle.**\n\n    Vol(chimney (inscribedTriangle R t α β γ) R)  =  Λ(α) + Λ(β) + Λ(γ)\n\nThe H4 tier's target, now stated on a triangle rather than on a union of three\nwedges.  The hypotheses are Milnor's: three positive acute angles summing to\n`π`.\n\nThe base is a.e. inside the open disk rather than pointwise inside it — the\nclosed inscribed triangle has its three vertices ON the circle, where the fibre\nmass is `⊤`.  That is exactly the a.e. form H4-2 was stated in\n(`hypVolume_chimney_of_ae_lt`), and here is where it is spent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.milnorWedges_ae_eq_inscribedTriangle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.milnorWedges_ae_eq_inscribedTriangle","kind":"theorem","line":400,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeTiling.lean#L400-L419","doc":"**THE TILING.**  Milnor's three wedges are the inscribed triangle, up to a\nnull set. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.volume_perpLine","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.volume_perpLine","kind":"theorem","line":383,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeTiling.lean#L383-L396","doc":"**An edge line is null.**  A line through the origin in the plane. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.perpFunctional_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.perpFunctional_apply","kind":"theorem","line":380,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeTiling.lean#L380-L381","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.perpFunctional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.perpFunctional","kind":"def","line":374,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeTiling.lean#L374-L378","doc":"The functional whose kernel is the edge line in direction `φ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.inscribedTriangle_subset_milnorWedges_of_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.inscribedTriangle_subset_milnorWedges_of_ne","kind":"theorem","line":307,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeTiling.lean#L307-L366","doc":"**The covering.**\n\nA point of the triangle that is off all three edge lines lies in one of the\nthree wedges.  The case split is on the signs of the three edge functionals;\n`perp_sign_relation` kills the all-positive and all-negative branches, and each\nof the six survivors is one application of `mem_wedgeAt_of_halfplanes`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.perp_sign_relation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.perp_sign_relation","kind":"theorem","line":284,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeTiling.lean#L284-L305","doc":"**The sign relation.**\n\nThe three edge functionals `w·v_t`, `w·v_{t+2γ}`, `w·v_{t+2γ+2α}` are three\nlinear functionals on a two-dimensional space, so they satisfy one relation;\n`α+β+γ = π` makes its coefficients `sin 2α, sin 2β, sin 2γ` — all POSITIVE for\nacute angles.  That positivity is the whole covering argument: it forbids the\ntwo sign patterns that would leave a point of the triangle in no sector. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.milnorWedges_subset_inscribedTriangle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.milnorWedges_subset_inscribedTriangle","kind":"theorem","line":250,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeTiling.lean#L250-L280","doc":"**Milnor's three wedges lie inside the inscribed triangle.**\n\nNine containments; each is one application of `wedgeAt_lt_chord_next` or\n`wedgeAt_lt_chord_prev`, except the three that are a wedge's own chord (by\ndefinition).  Two of the nine cross the first vertex and pick up the `2π`\nshift — the only place periodicity is used. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.cos_sub_cos_two_mul_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.cos_sub_cos_two_mul_add","kind":"theorem","line":242,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeTiling.lean#L242-L246","doc":"The elementary product-to-sum step behind every strict incidence below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.circlePoint_dot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.circlePoint_dot","kind":"theorem","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeTiling.lean#L235-L240","doc":"Testing a circle point against a chord direction sees only the angle\nbetween them. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.circlePoint","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.circlePoint","kind":"def","line":232,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeTiling.lean#L232-L233","doc":"The point of the circle of radius `R` at angle `a`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.measurableSet_inscribedTriangle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.measurableSet_inscribedTriangle","kind":"theorem","line":227,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeTiling.lean#L227-L230","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.inscribedTriangle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.inscribedTriangle","kind":"def","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeTiling.lean#L217-L225","doc":"**The triangle inscribed in the circle of radius `R`** with inscribed\nangles `(α, β, γ)` and first vertex at angle `t`, as the intersection of its\nthree chord half-planes.\n\nSee `inscribedTriangle_vertex_incidence` for the anchor that ties this\ndefinition to the triangle with the three named vertices. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.chordHalfplane_add_two_pi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.chordHalfplane_add_two_pi","kind":"theorem","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeTiling.lean#L211-L215","doc":"`2π`-periodicity of the chord half-plane, needed exactly twice below (the\ntwo wedges whose neighbour lies past the first vertex). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.measurableSet_chordHalfplane","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.measurableSet_chordHalfplane","kind":"theorem","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeTiling.lean#L207-L209","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.isOpen_chordHalfplane","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.isOpen_chordHalfplane","kind":"theorem","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeTiling.lean#L204-L205","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.chordHalfplane","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.chordHalfplane","kind":"def","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeTiling.lean#L198-L202","doc":"**The chord half-plane** — the open side, containing the circumcentre, of\nthe line through the chord whose midpoint direction is `θ` and which subtends\ncentral angle `2ψ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.wedgeAt_lt_chord_prev","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.wedgeAt_lt_chord_prev","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeTiling.lean#L170-L194","doc":"**The wedge fits inside the chord half-plane of its PREVIOUS neighbour** —\nthe mirror of `wedgeAt_lt_chord_next`, with the same certificate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.wedgeAt_lt_chord_next","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.wedgeAt_lt_chord_next","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeTiling.lean#L141-L168","doc":"**The wedge fits inside the chord half-plane of its NEXT neighbour.**\n\nThe identity in the header, item 2.  Note there is no `0 < R` hypothesis: the\nwedge's own chord slack `G₃` comes straight from membership, so a degenerate\n`R` makes the wedge empty and the statement vacuous rather than false. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.mem_wedgeAt_of_halfplanes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.mem_wedgeAt_of_halfplanes","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeTiling.lean#L113-L137","doc":"**The converse of `wedgeAt_upper` / `wedgeAt_lower`.**\n\nBeing strictly inside the chord half-plane and strictly on the correct side of\neach of the two edge lines puts a point in the wedge.  Together with\n`wedgeAt_upper` / `wedgeAt_lower` this says the wedge IS the intersection of\nthose three half-planes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.perp_sub_expand","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.perp_sub_expand","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeTiling.lean#L100-L105","doc":"Projection on `v_{θ−ψ}`, in the frame at `θ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.perp_add_expand","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.perp_add_expand","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeTiling.lean#L93-L98","doc":"Projection on `v_{θ+ψ}`, in the frame at `θ`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}